#!/usr/bin/env python3
from __future__ import annotations
"""
================================================================================
  EDGEQUANT  SENTINEL     (Telegram -> MetaTrader 5 execution engine)
  single file, no EA needed, no MT5 signal files
================================================================================

  WHAT IT DOES
    * watches your Telegram channels (matched by NAME, or by channel id)
    * LIMIT channels  -> places PENDING orders (limit / stop) and waits
    * MARKET channels -> always execute at the current broker market price;
      entry prices/ranges are informational and never become pending orders
    * MARKET-channel signals expire after 5 minutes
    * every entry price gets 2 LAYERS (2 orders) - always:
           layer 1 : Dashboard-configurable quick TP (default +50 pips)
           layer 2 : TP3 (or last available signal TP), moved 10 pips toward entry
           SL      : exactly the SL written in the message (never shifted);
                     no SL in the message -> automatic 50 pips SL
    * TRADE JOURNAL: every order + how it ended (TP / SL / BE / cancelled /
      rejected) with a per-channel win %  ->  --journal / EDGEQUANT-JOURNAL.bat
    * TELEGRAM NOTIFICATIONS: pending order filled, TP, SL, break-even
    * pending entries use the direction-based 10-pip shift; signal SL is unchanged
    * optional BE is OFF by default; when ON, the trigger defaults to +50 pips
    * handles channel updates: "Change All Sell Trades To TP 4135",
      "Change ... To BE", "Cancel pending orders", "Close all", "Close half"
    * duplicate guard, journal file, live-confirmation, DRY-RUN test mode

  QUICK START
    1) enter each client's own Telegram API ID/hash in LOGIN -> API SETUP
       (Windows DPAPI storage; local environment variables remain a fallback)
    2) test with:   EDGEQUANT-TEST.bat    (offline self test, no trading)
       and:         EDGEQUANT-DEBUG.bat   (prints every message, no trading)
    3) select joined sources, run TEST RUN, then use the account/risk LIVE gate
       from the desktop app before any real orders

  requirements:  pip install -r requirements.txt
================================================================================
"""

